1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,707
A tax incentive can
improve your return.

2
00:00:02,747 --> 00:00:05,859
But can it turn a weak location
into a good investment?

3
00:00:06,009 --> 00:00:11,283
Here's who qualifies, who actually benefits, and
what's left after location and execution costs.

4
00:00:11,433 --> 00:00:13,832
In El Salvador,
qualifying new investments

5
00:00:13,832 --> 00:00:19,269
in San Salvador's defined Historic Center may
receive up to ten years of income-tax relief.

6
00:00:19,309 --> 00:00:23,346
That's a specific regime for a
specific area, not a nationwide rule.

7
00:00:23,386 --> 00:00:25,477
And not every
business qualifies.

8
00:00:25,627 --> 00:00:27,051
Start with three checks.

9
00:00:27,091 --> 00:00:29,369
Location: inside the
defined perimeter.

10
00:00:29,369 --> 00:00:31,945
One block outside can
change the answer.

11
00:00:31,985 --> 00:00:37,182
Investment: an eligible activity, such as food,
lodging, or restoration, above the minimum.

12
00:00:37,222 --> 00:00:40,462
Approval: the Planning Authority
must qualify the project.

13
00:00:40,462 --> 00:00:42,152
No approval, no benefit.

14
00:00:42,302 --> 00:00:43,770
Then ask who receives it.

15
00:00:43,810 --> 00:00:47,380
Owner, operator, and developer
are often different companies.

16
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:51,566
A landlord's qualification doesn't
automatically cut a tenant's taxes.

17
00:00:51,716 --> 00:00:55,455
Here's a simplified, hypothetical
annual comparison, after tax.

18
00:00:55,495 --> 00:00:58,067
Thirty thousand dollars
of assumed tax savings,

19
00:00:58,067 --> 00:01:03,231
minus twenty-four thousand in added after-tax
occupancy costs, leaves six thousand a year.

20
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:05,893
It leaves out other costs,
timing, and risk.

21
00:01:05,893 --> 00:01:09,759
It's not a Salvadoran tax
calculation or a promised return.

22
00:01:09,909 --> 00:01:14,576
Demand, permits, utilities,
and opening delays can erase a thin advantage.

23
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:18,503
Underwrite the base case without incentives,
and show the benefit separately.

24
00:01:18,653 --> 00:01:20,912
That's the work Aurora
does on the ground:

25
00:01:20,912 --> 00:01:26,048
verify eligibility, test the site, and model
the real cost to open, before capital moves.

26
00:01:26,198 --> 00:01:30,686
Follow Aurora for the economics behind
expansion — not just the headline incentives.

27
00:01:30,726 --> 00:01:34,493
Next: who receives the benefit —
the owner, operator, or developer?
